# - Wikipedia FR, Alkpote article (opened 2026-10-20): born February 3, 1981 in the 10th arrondissement of Paris, French rapper of Tunisian origin; joined Unite 2 Feu in 1998 at 17, group album Haine, misere et crasse in 2006; solo Neochrome 2006; Sucez-moi avant l album in November 2007; L Empereur contre-attaque on March 19, 2012; Orgasmixtape April 2014 and volume 2 on May 11, 2015; Tenebreuse Musique with Butter Bullets January 2016; Sadisme et Perversion with DJ Weedim June 24, 2016; Les Marches de l empereur July 7, 2017 with Vald, Biffty, Iron Sy, MZ and Niska; opening slots for Gucci Mane in France June and July 2017; Inferno April 27, 2018, presented as third album; Monarchie Absolue clip with Bilal Hassani October 10, 2019; master cheesemaker diploma celebrated November 8, 2019 with Philippe Katerine; Ogre announced June 7, 2021 for July 9, 2021; LSDC February 3, 2023, subtitle Le Spectacle Doit Continuer, entirely produced by Tarik Azzouz, tracklist with Charge (feat. Kai du M); Rejouissances May 22, 2025 produced by Pandrezz; Les Ultimes Marches de l Empereur released as an album February 13, 2026 with 17 tracks; a shared album Jugement dernier with Tractopelle Musik announced for May 6, 2026. Full album tracklists for L Empereur, L Empereur contre-attaque, Sadisme et Perversion, Inferno, Monument, Ogre, LSDC and Rejouissances were read on that page.
# - PAN M 360, L Astral archives (search result, 2026-10-20): Al K-Pote who became Alkpote, who proclaimed himself the Emperor, born in 1981 in Paris under the name Atef Kahlaoui and raised in Evry. Used only to document the birth year conflict and the self proclaimed Emperor styling.
# - OTOTOY, Alkpote Vie rapide release page (opened 2026-10-20): seven tracks listed, track 1 Intro putrefaction credited to Alkpote and DJ Blax (2:06), then Pharaon, Vieillasse, Technologie seche, Sucepute, Noix de Saint-Jacques, and track 7 Hennesy credited to Alkpote, Luv Resval and Savage Toddy. The page shows no release date.
# - YouTube, Digestif auto generated audio (search result, 2026-10-20): provided by Arista France, from Monument, 2019 Sony Music Entertainment France, released November 8, 2019. Used only for the Monument release date.
# Note on method: the Deezer biography gives 1991 as the birth year while Wikipedia and PAN M 360 give 1981. This profile prints both and decides neither. No opened source gives Alkpote a bouyon recording. His documented links to this site are the DJ Blax credit on Vie rapide, the Kai Du M collaboration on LSDC, and Niska among the guests of Les Marches de l Empereur.

